-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  exe_build_errors.pcpp - Build kind: a link error mapped back

  An external routine no library defines fails at the link (ZB0016, the
  linker's own words), reported at the .pcpp line that calls it (the
  linker's referenced-by note, mapped like clang's locations). Debug only:
  the linker reads that line from the objects' debug info, which the other
  levels strip.
*******************************************************************************/

module exe exe_build_errors;

/*
  @@test
    kind error
    opt debug
  @@end
*/

routine clink exe_missing_symbol(): int32; external;

begin
  println("{}", exe_missing_symbol()); // ERROR ZB0016: exe_missing_symbol
end.
